92186441395 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441432 1079 #uuid "da43aee3-09a1-5940-8ad9-f3914ca15293" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441433 1075 #edb/ref 17592186441404 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441433 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441433 1077 "field-1" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441433 1078 #edb/ref 17592186441404 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441433 1079 #uuid "dbfacd55-1c0e-5862-bb80-6a63da7af696" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186441392 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186441402 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186441406 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186441407 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186441415 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441434 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441434 1077 "selection" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441434 1078 #edb/ref 17592186441392 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441434 1079 #uuid "f11adb4f-a6df-5572-a829-d227a29ca6f0" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441435 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441429 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441435 1069 "q-165432" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441435 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441435 1071 "![](images/db/dbf4056d9e2709bd959f4b8b79168941247af16ed1ae1b5dceb716cabe424830.png)\n\nWhat are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola shown above?" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441435 1072 #uuid "165f408f-fdbf-512c-a0a1-ee39f4be587e" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441435 1074 "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(3,4)$ and passes through the point $(2,3).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(3,4)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =4p(y-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(2,3),$ we substitute $x=2$ and $y=3$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2-3)^{2} & =4p(3-4) \\\\ 1 & =4p(-1) \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =-(y-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =-(0-4) \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm 2+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are $1$ and $5.$" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441436 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441426 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441436 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441432 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441436 1069 "q-251823" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441436 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441436 1071 "![](images/15/1500cb3f15e5a32229c861a7b5dcc19e06de0cd6757c8a872f5eb14ad6cb32de.png)\n\n**From top to bottom**, the **exact** values of the $y$-intercepts of the parabola shown above are{{field-1}}\nand \n{{field-2}}." 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441436 1072 #uuid "4260057c-f969-5185-9095-04c56e87e760" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441436 1074 "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-1,4)$ and passes through the point $(3,0).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(-1,4)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y-4)^{2}=4p(x+1).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(3,0),$ we substitute $x=3$ and $y=0$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-4)^{2} & =4p(3+1) \\\\ 16 & =4p(4) \\\\ p & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =4(x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =4(0+1) \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =4 \\\\ y-4 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2+4 \\\\ y & =2,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the $y$-intercepts are $6$ and  $2.$" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441437 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441421 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441437 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441422 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441437 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441423 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441437 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441433 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441437 1069 "q-251439" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441437 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441437 1071 "**From top to bottom**, the points of intersection of the parabola ${y}^{2}-12x-2y-8=0$ with the $y$-axis are $A$ and $B.$ Find the coordinates of $A$ and $B.$\n\n$A(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)\\,$ and $\\,B(${{field-3}}$,$\n{{field-4}}$)$" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441437 1072 #uuid "48d7d71f-4c73-5bda-b5f4-b80929ee461c" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441437 1074 "When the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we set $x=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-12(0)-2y-8 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-2y-8 & =0 \\\\ (y+2)(y-4) & =0 \\\\ y & =-2,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the intersection points, from top to bottom, are $(0,4)$ and $(0,-2).$" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441438 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441424 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441438 1069 "q-73764" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441438 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441438 1071 "Find the point of intersection of the parabola\n$(y-9)^{2}=-3x$\nwith the $x$-axis." 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441438 1072 #uuid "906c2725-0c67-5b11-96ab-a36547c9a017" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441438 1074 "When the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-9)^{2} & =-3x \\\\ 81 & =-3x \\\\ x & =-27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $x$-axis at $(-27,0).$" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441439 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441425 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441439 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441428 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441439 1069 "q-251826" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441439 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441439 1071 "![](images/0e/0e95f9087b5b607f2d33d49c0f5db123eede589e53adc94747f3a33c1fe68f90.png)\n\n**From top to bottom**, the **exact** values of the $y$-intercepts of the parabola shown above are{{field-1}}\nand \n{{field-2}}." 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441439 1072 #uuid "a25c3b40-7f3b-57d8-a341-b7f66aac34c1" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441439 1074 "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-8,-1)$ and passes through the point $(-6,1).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(-8,-1)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y+1)^{2}=4p(x+8).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-6,1),$ we substitute $x=-6$ and $y=1$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1+1)^{2} & =4p(-6+8) \\\\ 4 & =4p(2) \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =2(x+8).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =2(0+8) \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ y+1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{16} \\\\ y & =\\pm 4-1 \\\\ y & =-5,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the $y$-intercepts are $3$ and  $-5.$" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441440 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441430 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441440 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441431 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441440 1069 "q-251434" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441440 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441440 1071 "The parabola ${y}^{2}-3x+12y+36=0$ intersects the $x$-axis at the point$\\,(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441440 1072 #uuid "af6bef8d-9bda-5865-8318-f03b8c8ed1c7" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441440 1074 "When the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-3x+12y+36 & =0 \\\\ (0)^{2}-3x+12(0)+36 & =0 \\\\ -3x+36 & =0 \\\\ -3x & =-36 \\\\ x & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $x$-axis at $(12,0).$" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441441 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441427 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441441 1069 "q-73837" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441441 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441441 1071 "![](images/19/19895cff608c6c9fce2598b235b5415ac2856ccf508f11df52545672918ad6f7.png)\n\nWhat is the $y$-intercept of the parabola shown above?" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441441 1072 #uuid "baa62b58-d974-5e44-ba9b-341e234529fa" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441441 1074 "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-2,-5)$ and passes through the point $(1,4).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(-2,-5)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(x+2)^{2}=4p(y+5).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(1,4),$ we substitute $x=1$ and $y=4$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1+2)^{2} & =4p(4+5) \\\\ 9 & =4p(9) \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)^{2} & =y+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0+2)^{2} & =y+5 \\\\ 4 & =y+5 \\\\ y & =4-5 \\\\ y & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $-1.$" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441442 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441434 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441442 1069 "q-14280" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441442 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441442 1071 "Find the points of intersection of the parabola ${y}^{2}=-8(x-16)$ with the $y$-axis." 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441442 1072 #uuid "d5da328f-bab5-5074-ba79-45d8e6dffb79" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true] [17592186441442 1074 "When the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we set $x=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =-8(0-16) \\\\ {y}^{2} & =128 \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{128} \\\\ y & =\\pm 8\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $y$-axis at $(0,8\\sqrt{2})$ and $(0,-8\\sqrt{2}).$" 13194139534860 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0153ff6d-d05a-56ce-9b58-02c01757d0ac" 17592186441391 "answer-05b4bc6f-6eae-58f3-bd4e-a6df1a6e19f7" 17592186441392 "answer-15ab6d36-955b-5319-b4c2-4ceabe2971b7" 17592186441393 "answer-161002e7-3475-55d1-bf33-13e031fadd4a" 17592186441394 "answer-199f0fce-6ad5-5b52-bb36-a5c2e347b81d" 17592186441395 "answer-2021e1ee-a186-5932-a314-361aeb983eb5" 17592186441396 "answer-23b9a138-ccef-5b44-bdde-523564d8cad9" 17592186441397 "answer-26111051-d566-5d79-af8c-be170c78e32b" 17592186441398 "answer-3326bfbc-602b-5b97-a232-910eb4540d34" 17592186441399 "answer-3e9d1839-ab38-5603-9316-98bd943923cc" 17592186441400 "answer-4134ea6b-accb-5265-8339-c07c21944ba0" 17592186441401 "answer-549b8f34-438a-55fd-81c8-cc57361533ee" 17592186441402 "answer-557f7731-a814-5f95-8ddd-ff3a6a627548" 17592186441403 "answer-59d1c638-bc43-5894-9c3f-b999d8f59e6d" 17592186441404 "answer-6ec967a6-45c9-582d-b788-eca41cd0c25a" 17592186441405 "answer-75638e1e-4fe2-5380-80d6-466225c94b00" 17592186441406 "answer-7ea9ba4a-4b8b-5bad-a45e-00c2f7caa19d" 17592186441407 "answer-8056f24c-ed86-5bbd-af9e-159b07e24646" 17592186441408 "answer-862218b9-e397-5b8f-8db7-eedde7bba86f" 17592186441409 "answer-9e728a1e-a0dc-5359-8857-cc5f28c3dca6" 17592186441410 "answer-a5b77d34-ec2b-5142-964b-faad40063dd1" 17592186441411 "answer-ace6d14a-2a71-536b-8bbd-cd9914aff9ed" 17592186441412 "answer-bf011f4b-fdf9-543e-b412-3cda9fe4fcd1" 17592186441413 "answer-c1fd71a3-f959-5632-b94a-c770e9c6d2a3" 17592186441414 "answer-c47ad941-a4b2-5c3c-af7a-07dadfbe2daa" 17592186441415 "answer-c7aaabf2-9b3d-50fb-a39a-20b69f5186a6" 17592186441416 "answer-cb0b6c80-8dbc-56a7-a1a0-d14593c8129b" 17592186441417 "answer-d6831979-452b-5430-b4b7-e4fc46bb3bee" 17592186441418 "answer-ddf67998-b0d8-57b1-bbac-1c4711ac29d3" 17592186441419 "answer-faf3532c-56de-5ea6-8e58-fe9e6cec5cac" 1759218